=begin pod

=head1 NAME

B<QueryOS> - Provides a class and an executable, C<query-os>, to list OS details

=head1 SYNOPSIS

=begin code :lang<raku>
use QueryOS;
my $o = QueryOS.new; # <== alternatively: 'OS.new'
say $o.version-name  # OUTPUT: «debian␤»
=end code

=head1 DESCRIPTION

B<QueryOS> is a module that provides a class, C<QueryOS> (and its alias, C<OS>), with methods and
attributes to simplify module authors' porting their work to various
operating systems by identifying important system discriminators. The
module relies on the attributes of Raku's C<$*USER>, C<$*DISTRO>, and 
C<$*KERNEL> variables and parses out additional details in parts of 
those attributes.

Current attributes and methods are:

=item name           - from C<$*DISTRO.name>
=item version        - from C<$*DISTRO.version>
=item version-name   - text part of C<$*DISTRO.name>
=item version-serial - number part of C<$*DISTRO.name>
=item is-linux
=item is-windows
=item is-macos

=head1 List of known DISTRO names:

=item debian
=item gentoo
=item macos
=item mswin
=item suse
=item ubuntu

=head1 Example use in your code

In order to provide multi-OS use of your code there are
often times you need to take different paths or options
depending on the OS. Following is a generic code section
for doing that:

=begin code
use QueryOS;
my $os = OS.new;
if is-linux {
    ; # some Linux-only action
}
elsif is-macos {
    ; # some MacOS-only action
}
elsif is-windows {
    ; # some Windows-only action
}
else {
    note qq:to/HERE/;
    WARNING: Unknown OS. Please file an issue with module 'QueryOS'
             and provide information on what OS is being used
             and what you are trying to do that is unique for
             your OS.

             Also file an issue with this module's author.
    HERE
}
=end code

=head1 Example binary use for current OS details:

When I execute C<query-os q> on my system I get:

=begin code
This program is currently running on:

    Host:           bigtom
    User:           tbrowde
    Distro:         debian*
    Version name:   bullseye
    Version number: 11
    System:         x86_64

This module provides class 'QueryOS' (and its alias 'OS') whose attributes
provide details of the system to aid module
authors porting to multiple versions. See the
README for more information or use the 'list'
option to this program.

*NOTE: If the 'Distro' name is not recognized,
       it will be so stated in parentheses
       following the reported name.
=end code

